--==================================================================
--  Feed A Mosquito  |  Matcha LuaVM menu tab (UI.AddTab)
--
--  v10.14  -  respawn works: health is written in memory
--
--  WHY THE OLD RESPAWN DID NOTHING
--    Humanoid.Health = 0 and Character:BreakJoints() were both
--    measured as no-ops in this game - health stayed at its value and
--    the character stayed alive, because the server re-syncs
--    Humanoid.Health. Writing the field in memory sidesteps that.
--
--  VERIFIED THIS SESSION
--    memory_write("float", hum.Address + 0x184, -10)
--        before = 17116448, alive = true
--        after  = -10,       alive = false
--    So the write lands and the character dies.
--
--    The offset 0x184 is independently confirmed: a scan of
--    Address + 0..4096 found the health float at offset 388, which is
--    0x184. theo's offsets file also reports Health = 0x184.
--
--  THE OFFSET IS FETCHED, WITH A FALLBACK
--    At load this tries theo's offsets.hpp for the current Roblox
--    version and parses "Health = 0x...". If the fetch or the parse
--    fails it uses 0x184 and says so in the console, so you can see
--    which one it used. Offsets shift when Roblox updates, so the
--    fetch is the version-proof path and the fallback is the safety
--    net.
--
--  FAST RESPAWN  (inside Farm Kill, no separate toggle)
--    Fires when Farm Kill is on, you are alive, and the Character
--    holds NO Tool at all - no weapon, no egg being carried. That is
--    the "nothing in the queue and not holding my weapon" case.
--
--        1. remember your HumanoidRootPart CFrame
--        2. memory_write health to -10
--        3. watch for the new Character every 0.05 s
--        4. write the saved CFrame onto the new HumanoidRootPart
--
--    The game then runs its own respawn equip, which is the re-equip
--    you confirmed works. Nothing re-parents a Tool.
--
--  THE RESPAWN DELAY
--    The wait between death and respawn is the game's own
--    Players.RespawnTime, server-side. A client cannot shorten it. The
--    script prints that value on load so you know what to expect, and
--    returns you to your spot the moment the new character exists.
--
--  MENU
--      Main       Auto Health, Auto Collect
--      Farm       Farm Kill, Auto Hatch, Auto Equip Best
--      Egg Pickup Auto Pickup, TP Pickup (under egg), rarity filters
--
--  FARM KILL
--    AttackPart is the only thing written on the tool: shrink to 2
--    studs to end every contact, grow back to map size for a new one,
--    then PlaySound("SwingSound") + Attack on the LIVE tool actor from
--    the tool's ActorId value. No mouse input, nothing reparented.
--
--  AUTO HATCH
--    For every Runtime.Actors child named Egg_<uuid>:
--        .Events.Hatch:FireServer()
--    on a HATCH_RATE loop. Readiness cannot be read from here
--    (HatchReady is a RemoteEvent, not a value), so the server ignores
--    the passes that are not ready yet.
--
--  AUTO EQUIP BEST
--    Fires Runtime.Actors.Player_<UserId>.Events.PlaceBest on an
--    EQUIP_RATE loop. The path is built from LocalPlayer.UserId.
--
--  AUTO PICKUP / TP PICKUP
--    near range  - plain fireproximityprompt, instant
--    far range   - hop under the egg. Writing a CFrame below the floor
--      alone does not hold (the Humanoid collides with the baseplate
--      and physics resolves it back up), so CanCollide is turned off on
--      YOUR OWN character parts for the hop only, and restored on
--      return - plus again in stop() if it is called mid-hop.
--
--  PANEL
--      left  PANEL_X = 300   boss name, HP bar, hp / max
--
--  Stop with _G.FeedAMosquito.stop().
--==================================================================
